# Paths whose changes need the maintainer's review before they merge
# (docs/security.md, "CI, release and agents"). They are the control surface
# of CI, releases and agent sessions: a change here runs with repository
# secrets, publishes artifacts, or changes what every future agent session
# is told to do, so it must not land by auto-merge alone.
#
# The ruleset for `main` enforces this with "Require review from Code
# Owners". Everything not listed here keeps the ordinary auto-merge flow.

# Workflows, their helper scripts, this file and dependabot.
/.github/                         @tokuhirom

# Agent configuration: the session-start hook runs in every remote session,
# settings.json grants tool permissions, and the instructions steer every
# agent.
/.claude/                         @tokuhirom
/.agents/                         @tokuhirom
/AGENTS.md                        @tokuhirom
/docs/security.md                 @tokuhirom

# Scripts that run inside privileged CI jobs: the npm publish job (OIDC
# publish rights) and the ecosystem sweep's `collect` job (a write token),
# plus the classifier that decides whether CI builds at all.
/scripts/build-npm-package.sh     @tokuhirom
/scripts/prepare-npm-package.mjs  @tokuhirom
/scripts/ecosystem-ci.py          @tokuhirom
/scripts/ecosystem-ledger.sh      @tokuhirom
/scripts/ecosystem-sweep.py       @tokuhirom
/scripts/ecosystem_common.py      @tokuhirom
/scripts/ci-docs-only.sh          @tokuhirom
